  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "If ' $\\mathrm{D}$ ' be the foot of altitude, drawn from origin to the given line, then ${ }^{4} \\mathrm{D}^{\\prime}$ is the required point. Let $\\angle \\mathrm{OBA}=\\theta$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\tan \\theta=4 / 3$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\angle \\mathrm{DOA}=\\theta$\r\n$\\begin{aligned}\r\n&\\text { we have } \\quad \\mathrm{OD}=12 / 5 \\text { . }\\\\\r\n&\\text { If } D \\text { is }(h, k) \\text { then } h=O D \\cos \\theta, k=O D \\sin \\theta\\\\\r\n&\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{h}=36 / 25, \\mathrm{k}=48 / 25 .\r\n\\end{aligned}$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/5HcYlB5S4A4eT7SwEFhioTiafNfqqvnEdBOdZVh3PLM.original.fullsize.png\">",
